{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Allow student maintenance loans for distance-learning parent carers",
        "additional_details": "Children with autism, ADHD, anxiety, depression, physical disabilities or other additional needs may require ongoing care, supervision and emotional support. This can make attending university in person difficult or impossible. Distance learning offers parents the flexibility to study while meeting their children\u2019s needs, yet maintenance loans are generally unavailable to them. The Government should recognise these caring responsibilities and provide equal access to financial support.",
        "background": "Parents caring for children with additional needs may be unable to attend university in person. We believe they should have equal access to maintenance loans when studying online.",
